 this remainder). Empty competitor maxima are 0. Lists include title rows in both variants. with_titles adds only titles actually assigned to the returned elevation series.\",\r\n    \"interpretation\": \"Without titles: known_false_min=0 (karatsu-jikugumi2-p1), legitimate_max=0.21009416775716538 (kani-p38), holds=false. With assigned titles: both targeted false blocks have maximum 1, the control maximum stays 0.21009416775716538, holds=true on this census. This alternative envelope changes the measured object to a title-spanning area; it does not validate a demotion rule, classify all false blocks, or change ADR-046. shibata-p13 still has no competitor.\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"shibata_p13\": {\r\n    \"census\": {\r\n      \"fixture\": \"shibata-p13\",\r\n      \"lists\": 0,\r\n      \"blocks\": 1,\r\n      \"elevations\": 0,\r\n      \"titles_total\": 0\r\n    },\r\n    \"overlaps\": [\r\n      {\r\n        \"fixture\": \"shibata-p13\",\r\n        \"block_index\": 0,\r\n        \"evidence\": {\r\n          \"fixture\": \"tests/fixtures/section-import/textitems/shibata-p13.json\",\r\n          \"cacheFile\": \"dwg-shibata-fire.pdf\",\r\n          \"pageNumber\": 13\r\n        },\r\n        \"block_area_pt2\": 494167.03391230275,\r\n        \"competitors\": [],\r\n        \"maximum\": 0,\r\n        \"with_titles_maximum\": 0\r\n      }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"note\": \"No returned list or elevation competes with this false framing block. Both overlap maxima are 0.\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"region_definition\": {\r\n    \"units\": \"pt, +x right, +y down; bbox={left,top,right,bottom}; areas pt^2; ratios dimensionless\",\r\n    \"text_item_bbox\": {\r\n      \"horizontal\": \"[x,x+w] x [y-h,y]\",\r\n      \"rot_minus_90\": \"[x-h,x] x [y-w,y]; advance upwards, ascent towards negative x; abs(rot+90)<0.01 matches verticalRuns\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"section_list\": \"Envelope of actual parseTableRegion tableRows[].items including title row; returned lists only, including 0-candidate lists. No xStart/xEnd Infinity. Slab/wall row selection remains exactly as implemented; no extra vertical-run items added.\",\r\n    \"framing_block\": \"All AxisCandidate.positionPt extents of returned block xGrid/yGrid, mapped to page coordinates by xSequence.alongKey; includes 0-placement blocks. Only selectedBlocks after filtering/sorting count.\",\r\n    \"elevation\": \"Envelope of underlying original TextItems in adopted chain dimension tokens and labelsAtLevels of each returned resolved candidate. No titles. with_titles additionally unions glyphs of titles assigned to the same candidate.\",\r\n    \"degenerate\": \"No items => bbox null; zero area => degenerate true. Degenerate competitor intersection 0; degenerate block ratio would be null. No degenerate regions observed.\",\r\n    \"intersection\": \"max(0,min(right)-max(left))*max(0,min(bottom)-max(top)) divided by whole block area. Every returned block paired with every returned list/series on the same page.\",\r\n    \"titles_total\": \"Sum of titles.length over returned ElevationCandidate objects; excludes raw unmatched title texts and list/framing titles.\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"procedure\": {\r\n    \"input\": \"Sort all 36 textitems/*.json fixtures; TextPage={...fixture.page,items:fixture.items}; call all three parsers with defaults once per page.\",\r\n    \"canonical_hash\": \"Recursively sort object keys, omit undefined properties, retain array order; JSON.stringify without whitespace, UTF-8 SHA-256 of {lists,plan,elevations}. Numbers are unrounded.\",\r\n    \"instrumentation\": \"Exact temporary replacement pairs in instrumentation. WeakMap keyed by VerticalRun/Token retains original glyph identities; copied DimensionToken inherits them. tableRows capture before headerIndexes is associated with returned parseTableRegion results. Block object WeakMap at blocks.push is read only for returned plan.blocks. Elevation identity tracks chains, attached labels and actual assigned title tokens; only resolved candidates after withoutOverlaps count.\",\r\n    \"restoration\": \"Original bytes saved as base64 before instrumentation, restored byte-for-byte. All four before/after SHA-256 pairs match. All 36 parser output hashes match baseline with instrumentation and again after restoration.\",\r\n    \"retry_note\": \"First observer counted raw blocks.push calls and hit 2 vs 1 against returned blocks: parser prefers titled blocks. Observer corrected to object identity lookup of returned plan.blocks; no parser logic changed.\",\r\n    \"observer_source\": \"import fs from 'node:fs'\\nimport crypto from 'node:crypto'\\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict'\\nimport { parseSectionLists } from '../../src/lib/import/section-list/parse'\\nimport { parseFramingPlan } from '../../src/lib/import/framing-plan/parse'\\nimport { parseFrameElevations } from '../../src/lib/import/framing-plan/elevation'\\nconst dir = 'phases/44-drawing-set-assembly/'\\nconst report = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(dir+'step1-report.json','utf8'))\\nconst mode = process.argv[2]\\nconst canonical = (v:any):any => Array.isArray(v) ? v.map(canonical) : v && typeof v==='object' ? Object.fromEntries(Object.keys(v).sort().filter(k=>v[k]!==undefined).map(k=>[k,canonical(v[k])])) : v\\nconst hash = (v:any) => crypto.createHash('sha256').update(JSON.stringify(canonical(v))).digest('hex')\\nconst union = (boxes:any[]) => boxes.length ? {left:Math.min(...boxes.map(b=>b.left)),top:Math.min(...boxes.map(b=>b.top)),right:Math.max(...boxes.map(b=>b.right)),bottom:Math.max(...boxes.map(b=>b.bottom))} : null\\nconst area = (b:any) => b ? Math.max(0,b.right-b.left)*Math.max(0,b.bottom-b.top) : 0\\nconst itemBox = (i:any) => i.rot!==undefined && Math.abs(i.rot+90)<0.01 ? {left:i.x-i.h, right:i.x, top:i.y-i.w,bottom:i.y} : {left:i.x,right:i.x+i.w,top:i.y-i.h,bottom:i.y}\\nconst blockRegions = new WeakMap<object,any>()\\nlet page:any, current:any, pending:any\\nconst tokenItems = new WeakMap<object,any[]>(), series = new WeakMap<object,any>()\\nconst makeRegion = (items:any[]) => {const bbox=union(items.map(itemBox));return {bbox,degenerate:area(bbox)===0,item_indexes:[...new Set(items.map(i=>page.items.indexOf(i)))].sort((a:any,b:any)=>a-b)}}\\n;(globalThis as any).__census = {\\n  tokenItems,\\n  table(rows:any[],anchor:any) {pending={...makeRegion(rows.flatMap(r=>r.items)),title:anchor.titleText,row_count:rows.length}},\\n  list(result:any) {current.lists.push({...pending,index:current.lists.length,listKind:result.listKind,candidates:result.candidates.length,issue:result.issue??null})},\\n  block(block:any,alongKey:string) {const x=alongKey==='x'?block.xGrid.axes:block.yGrid.axes,y=alongKey==='y'?block.xGrid.axes:block.yGrid.axes;const bbox={left:Math.min(...x.map((a:any)=>a.positionPt)),right:Math.max(...x.map((a:any)=>a.positionPt)),top:Math.min(...y.map((a:any)=>a.positionPt)),bottom:Math.max(...y.map((a:any)=>a.positionPt))};blockRegions.set(block,{title:block.title??null,placements:block.placements.length,x_grid_along_key:alongKey,bbox,degenerate:area(bbox)===0})},\\n  series(candidate:any,chain:any[],labels:any[]) {series.set(candidate,{...makeRegion([...chain,...labels].flatMap(t=>tokenItems.get(t)!)),dimension_tokens:chain.map(t=>({text:t.text,x:t.x,y:t.y})),label_tokens:labels.map(t=>({text:t.text,x:t.x,y:t.y})),titleItems:[]})},\\n  title(candidate:any,title:any) {if(candidate)series.get(candidate).titleItems.push(...tokenItems.get(title)!)},\\n  resolved(candidates:any[]) {current.elevations=candidates.map((c,index)=>{const s=series.get(c),with_titles=makeRegion([...s.item_indexes.map((i:number)=>page.items[i]),...s.titleItems]);const {titleItems,...rest}=s;return {...rest,index,titles:c.titles,with_titles}})}\\n}\\nconst hashes:any={}, census:any[]=[], regions:any[]=[]\\nconst fixtures=fs.readdirSync('tests/fixtures/section-import/textitems').filter(f=>f.endsWith('.json')).sort()\\nassert.equal(fixtures.length,36)\\nfor(const file of fixtures){const raw=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('tests/fixtures/section-import/textitems/'+file,'utf8'));page={...raw.page,items:raw.items};current={fixture:file.replace('.json',''),evidence:{fixture:'tests/fixtures/section-import/textitems/'+file,cacheFile:raw.source.cacheFile,pageNumber:raw.source.page},lists:[],blocks:[],elevations:[]};const lists=parseSectionLists(page),plan=parseFramingPlan(page),elevations=parseFrameElevations(page);hashes[current.fixture]=hash({lists,plan,elevations});census.push({fixture:current.fixture,lists:lists.length,blocks:plan.blocks.length,elevations:elevations.elevations.length,titles_total:elevations.elevations.reduce((n,c)=>n+c.titles.length,0)});if(mode==='measured'){current.blocks=plan.blocks.map((b,index)=>({...blockRegions.get(b),index}));assert.ok(current.blocks.every(b=>b.bbox));assert.equal(current.lists.length,lists.length);assert.equal(current.blocks.length,plan.blocks.length);assert.equal(current.elevations.length,elevations.elevations.length);for(const r of [...current.lists,...current.elevations])assert.ok(r.item_indexes.every((i:number)=>i>=0));regions.push(current)}}\\nif(mode==='baseline'){report.parser_output_hashes=hashes;report.census={pages:census,summary:{list_pages:census.filter(p=>p.lists>0).length,block_pages:census.filter(p=>p.blocks>0).length,elevation_pages:census.filter(p=>p.elevations>0).length,multi_role_pages:census.filter(p=>[p.lists,p.blocks,p.elevations].filter(n=>n>0).length>1).length}};fs.writeFileSync(dir+'step1-report.json',JSON.stringify(report,null,2)+'\\\\n');console.log(report.census.summary)}\\nelse {assert.deepEqual(hashes,report.parser_output_hashes);if(mode==='measured'){fs.writeFileSync(dir+'.step1-regions.json',JSON.stringify(regions,null,2)+'\\\\n');console.log('36 instrumented output hashes identical; regions captured')}else console.log('36 restored output hashes identical')}\\n\",\r\n    \"bounds_note\": \"List envelopes are read-row bounds, not certified physical tables. Elevation bounds are glyph envelopes, not full frames. B1 used